        "questionDiagrams": [
          {
            "id": "p70-q24-a-diagram",
            "role": "question",
            "format": "tikz",
            "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"page 70, p70-q24-a-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.6cm,y=0.6cm,line cap=round,line join=round]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\pgfmathsetmacro{\\wallHeight}{9.93799368936}\n\\pgfmathsetmacro{\\groundDistance}{1.11188193176}\n\\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\n\\coordinate (T) at (0,\\wallHeight);\n\\coordinate (F) at (\\groundDistance,0);\n\\coordinate (C) at (1,1);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (0,10.3)--(O)--(2,0);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (O)--(1,0)--(C)--(0,1)--cycle;\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (T)--(F);\n\\node[black,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,anchor=west] at ($(T)!0.52!(F)$) {$10\\,\\mathrm{m}$};\n\\node[black,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,anchor=north,yshift=-2pt] at (0.5,0) {$1\\,\\mathrm{m}$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
            "src": null,
            "widthMm": 30,
            "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
            "overlayOf": null,
            "transparent": false,
            "axes": null,
            "spec": {
              "sourcePage": 70,
              "sourceRegion": "Question 24(a), left-hand side elevation",
              "description": "Vertical wall on the left, horizontal ground, and an unfilled unit square at their junction. A steep ladder touches the square's upper-right corner and reaches the wall above it and the ground beyond it. Coordinates reproduce a valid configuration of the stated model; no additional dimensions are printed.",
              "mathematics": "The cube's side elevation is a unit square. The ladder joins (0,H) to (D,0), where H≈9.93799368936 and D≈1.11188193176, with H²+D²=100 and 1/H+1/D=1, so it passes through (1,1).",
              "answerVisibility": "The diagram and its supplied 10 m and 1 m labels remain visible in the question edition."
            },
            "derived": false,
            "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
          }
        ],
        "children": [],
        "diagramPlacement": "beside-prompt",
        "answer": {
          "short": "Similar triangles give $y=\\frac1x$. Substituting into $(x+1)^2+(y+1)^2=100$ gives $x^4+2x^3-98x^2+2x+1=0$.",
          "worked": "Using Pythagoras’ theorem:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x+1)^2+(1+y)^2&=10^2.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing similar triangles:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{y}{1}&=\\frac{1}{x}\\\\y&=\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute, expand and multiply every term by $x^2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(x+1)^2+\\left(1+\\frac1x\\right)^2&=100\\\\x^2+2x+2+\\frac2x+\\frac1{x^2}&=100\\\\x^4+2x^3+2x^2+2x+1&=100x^2\\\\x^4+2x^3-98x^2+2x+1&=0.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      },
      {
        "id": "p70-q24-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Use an online calculator to find the height up the wall the ladder reaches to 2 decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1.11\\,\\mathrm{m}$ or $9.94\\,\\mathrm{m}$.",
          "worked": "The online calculator gives the positive roots $x\\approx0.1118819318$ or $x\\approx8.9379936894$. The negative roots do not represent this configuration.\nThe height up the wall is $x+1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}h&\\approx1.1118819318\\,\\mathrm{m}\\quad\\text{or}\\quad9.9379936894\\,\\mathrm{m}\\\\h&\\approx1.11\\,\\mathrm{m}\\quad\\text{or}\\quad9.94\\,\\mathrm{m}\\qquad\\text{(2 decimal places).}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
